   "unit_text": "The pinna collects sound signal1 from the environment, \nwhich passes through EAC and vibrates the TM (Fig. 29). \nVibrations of the TM are transmitted to the stapes footplate \nthrough the chain of ossicles.2 Vibrations of stapes footplate \nresult in the pressure changes in the labyrinthine fluids3 \n\nthat lead to movement of the basilar membrane and thus \nstimulate the hair cells of the organ of Corti. The IHC of cochlea \nact as transducers and convert the mechanical energy into \nelectrical impulses which travel along the auditory nerve. ",
